// The campaign snippet (../xhpcg_spmvm_ref_gem5fs.snippet) at this binary's PCs: the same
// labels and chains, every listed instruction the same, only moved.
// ROI (hpcg_roi.hpp): main() arms it right before the first timed CG call
// (main.cpp, hpcg_roi_armed), and ComputeSPMV marks only its first call after that:
// CG's first SpMV (Ap = A*p, before CG's loop), on the real matrix. ComputeSPMV calls
// ComputeSPMV_ref out of line (bl at 213cc) inside the ROI and tail-calls it (b at 2138c)
// otherwise, so a restore runs that one SpMV to roi_end_.
// Every HPCG ref snippet lists the same four indirect kernels, so the files share one
// layout; labels on code that does not run in the region are harmless.
// None of the four kernels is inlined in this build: ComputeSPMV, ComputeSYMGS and
// ComputeMG_impl reach them by bl or by a tail-call b, so the PCs below are the ones
// that execute.
// SpMV:         sum += cur_vals[j] * xv[cur_inds[j]]
// SYMGS:        sum -= currentValues[j] * xv[currentColIndices[j]]  (forward, then backward sweep)
// Restriction:  rcv[i] = rfv[f2c[i]] - Axfv[f2c[i]]
// Prolongation: xfv[f2c[i]] += xcv[i]
// xv is the x argument of each kernel (a different vector in SpMV and in SYMGS).
// ExchangeHalo, called by SpMV (bl at 2143c) and SYMGS, packs
// sendBuffer[i] = xv[elementsToSend[i]]; with 8 processes it runs inside the ROI, but it
// is not listed, as in the campaign snippet (hov does not offload it either, so the xv
// counts of ref and hov stay comparable).
